      },
      "text": "Section 1. E sta b lish m en t o f B oard. There is established, effective January 7,  \n1989, a board of three members to be appointed by the President to investigate  \nthis dispute. No member shall be pecuniarily or otherwise interested in any  \norganization of railroad employees or any carrier. The board shall perform its  \nfunctions subject to the availability of funds."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2584,
      "char_start": 1935,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:12664#sec2",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "Sec. 2.",
      "pdf_page": 181,
      "scope_id": "EO:12664#sec2",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "54 FR 959, PDF pages 181-181",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "784a3488bfca4ab1779e7158c0e4e7ba8c8ffe6a549a1be4434b3daf4fbfd502",
        "signing_date": "1989-01-06",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_12664.txt",
        "text_sha256": "697717bdb6e38a177ca8c077a8a404de3e624a53ae5ad49684d9330e5d1682a7",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1989-01-10/pdf/FR-1989-01-10.pdf"
      },
      "text": "Sec. 2. R ep o rt Within 30 days after creation of the board, the parties to the  \ndispute shall submit to the board final offers for settlement of the dispute.  \nWithin 30 days after submission of final offers for settlement of the dispute,  \nthe board shall submit a report to the President setting forth its selection of the  \nmost reasonable offer.\nSec. 3 .M a in ta in in g  C onditions. As provided by.Section 9A(h) of the Act, from  \nthe time a request to establish a board is made until 60 days after the board  \nmakes its report no change, except by agreement shall be made by the  \nparties in the conditions out of which the dispute arose."
    },
